{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:64bcfbee590df2ba","name":"Neural Inhibitor","source":{"id":"source:reference-64bcfbee590df2ba","title":"Neural Inhibitor","revision":19718,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:29:12Z","sha256":"6eab3d9f826b1dd30cb2d28370f12209f6ed50ee34452d062f0e208344ce271e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19718","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Neural%20Inhibitor&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-64bcfbee590df2ba","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Mennotor DAS-430 Neural Inhibitor is a powered, ranged weapon that uses some of the same technology as rail guns to propel a high-velocity dart at the target, which embeds itself into the skin. The dart then injects a special neurotoxin that can bring down even the toughest enemies.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When a living target is hit by an attack with a Neural Inhibitor, the target is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poisoned"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poisoned"}," and the dart makes an attack roll (1d20+5) against the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},". If the attack succeeds, the target moves -1 step down the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},". If the attack fails, the target does not move down the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},", but the dart's next attack gains a cumulative +1 bonus (so it attacks with 1d20+5 originally, 1d20+6 after the first failure, 1d20+7 after the second failure, etc.).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition"}," is considered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent"}," until the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poison"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poison"}," is treated, and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poison"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poison"}," makes an attack roll at the beginning of the target's turn until the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Poison"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Poison"}," is cured with a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Treat Injury"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Treat_Injury","referenceId":"reference:f1b9875c2302ce61"}," check. Once the target falls unconscious, the neurotoxin dissipates on its own. A Neural Inhibitor requires darts, and only can hold only one dart at a time. Each dart costs 5 credits.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weapon Type:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapons (Ranged)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapons_(Ranged)","referenceId":"reference:c954289d43de9110"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size:"]}," Medium\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 4,200\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 1d6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," Setting:"]}," NO\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Rate of Fire:"]}," Single-Shot\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 1 Kilogram\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Type:"]}," Piercing\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Illegal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Illegal"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Inaccurate:"]}," This weapon cannot fire at targets at Long ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"},".\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
